>...  The priest has a great advantage in that he can work blessed scrolls
>more reliably; he got his AC through this, and also genocided just about
>everything dangerous in the dungeon this way.

The priest isn't better at using blessed items, just at recognizing them.

>Teleported to level 45, and
>used a binary search to find the Wiz.  (Try looking at a mirror when blind.)

No binary search is needed.  The message changes from "below you" to "far below
you" at a distance of 10 levels from him.

>...Stendhal ascended to the stronghold level, and was
>faced with a problem: he had no way of crossing the trapdoors in the castle,
>because his ring of levitation had become cursed, and he didn't want to put it
>on.  At this point, Stendhal forsook his usual reason, and tried to polymorph
>himself into a giant bat and fly across.  Unfortunately, he did not know two
>things:
>1) Polymorphing into a giant bat destroys body armor.
>2) Giant bats have a very low carrying capacity.

If this happens to you, try a vampire lord.  They can fly and are humanoid so
they can wear armor.

Also, you can save items from being cursed by putting them in a sack.  (Don't
use a bag of holding; bags of holding sometimes lose objects if the bag gets
cursed.)

>...He became a new man.  It
>seemed, though, that the new man did not have the old one's fire resistance:

>"The flames of Hell burn you to a crisp.  The flames of Hell burn you to a
>crisp --More--
>This looped infinitely.  I had to kill the program from another shell, &
>didn't even get to make the high score list.  (I was running Patchlevel 4).

The looping will be fixed when patchlevel 5 comes out.  (Sigh...) I don't
understand how you lost fire resistance though (unless a gremlin hit you);
polymorphing does _not_ cause you to lose intrinsics.

>2) Is Stormbringer better than Excalibur?

It drains a level, so when the Wizard teleports away he can only heal up to his
newer, lower maximum.

>3) What is a magic lamp, and how do I use it?

It shows up as a "lamp" until you #rub it.  On a 1/5 chance (or always, if it's
blessed), the djinni will give you a wish.  (Other results are possible.)

>5) Why?

1) Why not?
2) Because.
